# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mektep Prayer
#
# Every value here is optional. With an empty .env the app still runs: it uses
# the keyless Aladhan API with the Diyanet calculation method, and falls back to
# calculating times locally if it cannot reach the network.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Diyanet (official times) ----------------------------------------------
# An account for awqatsalah.diyanet.gov.tr. With these set, a "Diyanet place"
# picker appears in the settings drawer; choose a district there and its times
# come straight from Diyanet.
#
# Mind the quota. A Standard-role account gets five requests per day PER
# ENDPOINT, and there is no yearly endpoint — /PrayerTime/Monthly returns the
# current month and takes no month parameter. The app therefore caches every
# response to disk and fills the rest of the year by calculation. Keep the
# .cache volume mounted (see docker-compose.yml) or every restart re-spends the
# day's allowance.
DIYANET_EMAIL=
DIYANET_PASSWORD=

# Requests per endpoint per day the app will spend. Held under the documented
# limit of 5 so a bad day cannot lock the account out.
DIYANET_DAILY_BUDGET=4

# Override only if Diyanet moves the service.
# DIYANET_BASE_URL=https://awqatsalah.diyanet.gov.tr

# --- Upstream services (all keyless) ---------------------------------------
# Override these only to point at a proxy or a mirror.
# ALADHAN_BASE_URL=https://api.aladhan.com/v1
# OPEN_METEO_BASE_URL=https://api.open-meteo.com/v1
# OPEN_METEO_GEOCODING_URL=https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1

# --- Server ----------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=3000
